{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations","id":1118006,"title":"Pijavica and Protean: Discipline Alterations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-18T17:25:26-07:00","id":1118006,"title":"Pijavica and Protean: Discipline Alterations","content":"Hey all, Korogra here! After reading A Thousand Years Of Night and taking an even greater interest in the Pijavica, my mind kept coming back to the fact that they had Protean as their signature Discipline and a thought occurred to me: Protean had to function differently for the Pijavica than it did for the Gangrel in order to more effectively reflect the nature of their particular brand of the Curse, and I'm not talking about them just having creepy blood-worm themed Devotions. Sure at its core their Protean would operate under the same principle; being shape changing powers that give the Beast a more material expression of Itself, but that's wherein the differences would rapidly become apparent. Much like how the Akhem-Urtu possessing unique versions of existing Utterance powers in Mummy; Protean when used by the Pijavica carries with it abilities unique to their clan. Now what would these abilities be? I'm not entirely sure, but I am already starting to get a vague mental picture. I do think that the Discipline's five levels would still more or less function similarly to how they do when the Gangrel or other vampires use Protean, but at the same time they do not.. perhaps they have the same powers for each level, but instead of a focus on animals and how the Beast emulates them, perhaps it deals with blood and flesh-warping? Now I'm not sure how this would work and will probably build a homebrewed version of Protean for the Pijavica, but I would love help and input from you guys! If you could give your own theories and ideas of how this would work, I would immensely appreciate it. I'm sure that we could all come up with something really cool! As always, I look forward to seeing what you guys think on this conundrum! Thanks and have a wonderful day!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T20:01:44-07:00","id":1118038,"title":"","content":"It has been said by others on this forum that the pijavica are a VtR expy of the tzimisce so maybe something similar to fleashcraft but more goopy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T20:32:08-07:00","id":1118046,"title":"","content":"I personally think all clans should have slightly tweaked aesthetics for their discipline use, so it's very easy for me to imagine that the aesthetic of Protean when used by Pijavica would be more like The Thing than an animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T20:37:07-07:00","id":1118048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1118038#post1118038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been said by others on this forum that the pijavica are a VtR expy of the tzimisce so maybe something similar to fleashcraft but more goopy</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've made that connection and I think that it would be pretty cool to partially meld the flesh and bone manipulation of Viccissitude with the free flowing shape changing of Protean to reflect the metamorphic nature of the Pijavica","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T20:42:16-07:00","id":1118049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1118046#post1118046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think all clans should have slightly tweaked aesthetics for their discipline use, so it's very easy for me to imagine that the aesthetic of Protean when used by Pijavica would be more like The Thing than an animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, the potential is limitless. While I'm not a fan of the Thing as a franchise, that does give me an idea for Devotions relying on Protean/Animalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T17:47:10-07:00","id":1118325,"title":"","content":"Well, maybe the Gangrel just have a more limited vision. Claws and fur, burrowing and fangs. The ingredients of a mammal, usually. On the periphery, reptiles and fish. These are all from Chordates, mostly Vertebrates. In the rarest cases, arthropods, which still keeps you in Bilatera.<br /> <br /> But, there is a great big world of other animals out there: Molluscs, Annelids, Flatworms, Nematodes, Cnidarians, Sponges, and Comb Jellies. Among this group, the Pijavica life-cycle and body plans are actually fairly mundane.<br /> <br /> That's just in Animalia, and the outer bounds of Animalia has become a slightly fuzzier concept lately than it used to be.<br /> <br /> Choanoflagellates are kissing cousins of animals, and, though unicellular, some form colonial systems, like very, very early animals.<br /> <br /> Further afield, fungi (mushrooms, yeasts, and molds) are not plants, but are more their whole own thing. Like animals, they are heterotrophs (eating outside material) and share the material chitin with insects. They lack motility, though some spores move with flagella, in a manner similar to animal sperm, rather than like protists. Molecular Biology pretty much now says they have several traits in common with animals, and are definitely closer to animals than plants. (This, though, is a bit like saying Mercury is closer to Venus than Mars. It's largely true, but it's still not close.)<br /> <br /> So, just widen the palette Protean uses, and you've got the Pijavica explained.<br /> <br /> The bigger question might be: why don't Gangrel ever seem to use animal traits from a wider group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T23:22:39-07:00","id":1118416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1118325#post1118325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The bigger question might be: why don't Gangrel ever seem to use animal traits from a wider group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably has to do with how vampires supernaturally resonate/sympathize with predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T09:54:15-07:00","id":1118597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1118325#post1118325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe the Gangrel just have a more limited vision. Claws and fur, burrowing and fangs. The ingredients of a mammal, usually. On the periphery, reptiles and fish. These are all from Chordates, mostly Vertebrates. In the rarest cases, arthropods, which still keeps you in Bilatera.<br /> <br /> But, there is a great big world of other animals out there: Molluscs, Annelids, Flatworms, Nematodes, Cnidarians, Sponges, and Comb Jellies. Among this group, the Pijavica life-cycle and body plans are actually fairly mundane.<br /> <br /> That's just in Animalia, and the outer bounds of Animalia has become a slightly fuzzier concept lately than it used to be.<br /> <br /> Choanoflagellates are kissing cousins of animals, and, though unicellular, some form colonial systems, like very, very early animals.<br /> <br /> Further afield, fungi (mushrooms, yeasts, and molds) are not plants, but are more their whole own thing. Like animals, they are heterotrophs (eating outside material) and share the material chitin with insects. They lack motility, though some spores move with flagella, in a manner similar to animal sperm, rather than like protists. Molecular Biology pretty much now says they have several traits in common with animals, and are definitely closer to animals than plants. (This, though, is a bit like saying Mercury is closer to Venus than Mars. It's largely true, but it's still not close.)<br /> <br /> So, just widen the palette Protean uses, and you've got the Pijavica explained.<br /> <br /> The bigger question might be: why don't Gangrel ever seem to use animal traits from a wider group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the previous post stated. Protean does have a supernatural connection to predatory animals, and the mechanics limit what sort of creatures can be imitated. Still, such things like fungi and other microorganisms would be cool for the Pijavica","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T16:01:32-07:00","id":1119097,"title":"","content":"This would be an interesting avenue for a Bloodline to explore. I have some ideas about Pijavica bloodlines and, say, insects, but I'm borrowing a computer right now and cannot expand my ideas properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T17:09:45-07:00","id":1119364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1119097#post1119097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be an interesting avenue for a Bloodline to explore. I have some ideas about Pijavica bloodlines and, say, insects, but I'm borrowing a computer right now and cannot expand my ideas properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you have the time, I would love to hear it. Just today I thought of a particularly deliciously Tzimisce esque devotion that essentially recreates The Corruption from Dead Space. I'll post it after my shift tonight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T04:06:25-07:00","id":1119455,"title":"","content":"Well, other than something like a poison ability or maybe a variation of spider webbing, what abilities can you put down that aren't already covered by reflavoring Protean? Lets say that one of the Pijavica uses prtean to make extra arms and a bloody hand-knife. How is that different from the mechanics of Prehensile Tail and Claw? <br /> <br /> Here's the thing. Its pretty trivial to reflavor Protean features into something other than the classic bat, wolf and reptile. So, going by just rough mechanics, what kind of feature is lacking? Protean 3 is admittedly trickier to do, since that requires basically creating new forms each time from the ground up (which is a pain in the arse for anything not on the errata animal list), but what about anything else?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T04:14:58-07:00","id":1119458,"title":"","content":"Even if you come up with powers that aren't reflavourings of Protean, they could easily fit in as Clan-only Devotions or even Merits...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T17:31:06-07:00","id":1119694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1119455#post1119455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, other than something like a poison ability or maybe a variation of spider webbing, what abilities can you put down that aren't already covered by reflavoring Protean? Lets say that one of the Pijavica uses prtean to make extra arms and a bloody hand-knife. How is that different from the mechanics of Prehensile Tail and Claw?<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. Its pretty trivial to reflavor Protean features into something other than the classic bat, wolf and reptile. So, going by just rough mechanics, what kind of feature is lacking? Protean 3 is admittedly trickier to do, since that requires basically creating new forms each time from the ground up (which is a pain in the arse for anything not on the errata animal list), but what about anything else?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><u>Any of the following abilities would need to be written up with game mechanics in mind and might not be possible, anyway, but are worth consideration:</u><br /> <br /> Lacking a skeleton might allow squeezing through extremely small openings and would make you virtually impossible to tie up or handcuff. It also ma give the option of enveloping another creature completely.<br /> <br /> Carnivorous sponges (which sound like a bad horror movie concept, but exist on the continental shelf off Antarctica) hunt by producing a very sticky substance which traps prey on their surface and then absorb nutrients at their leisure. This sticky stuff is strong enough to hold prey in very cold salt water. If used on dry land, it would make it virtually impossible for prey to escape.<br /> <br /> Coral and some molluscs are able to create hard, stone-like structures around their bodies. A vampire who is expecting to enter torpor could create such a shell before merging with the earth, making for a very durable haven.<br /> <br /> Jellyfish and flatworms often have no heart, using a system distantly similar to peristalsis to push nutrients through their bodies. Some animals have no circulatory system at all; blood (if they have clearly differentiated blood, many just use sea water) just diffuses through their body. How would you stake a vampire with this set-up?<br /> <br /> Brains are another optional organ, common among vertebrates, but not especially vital among other animals. Some have a bundle of nerves that kind of resemble a brain, some just don't, and contract out all their nerve activity to individual body parts. This is why octopus tentacles keep moving and reacting to touch after removal. If a vampire had this feature, would beheading matter?<br /> <br /> If you want to start a shouting match at a dinner party full of biologists, take on firm stand on whether there are any animals that do not feel pain. It is... contentious, to say the least. But, for story purposes, it could allow to you argue for using Protean to remove the concept of wound penalties.<br /> <br /> If you want some ideas for some immunities to different types of damage, the list is pretty long, just check out the wikipedia article on extremophiles. Picrophilus has an optimal growth pH of .2, approaching the acidity of battery acid. Strain 121 (which arguably would not eligible since it's not quite an animal... it is an Archaean, but...) can reproduce at 121centigrade. Yep, that's well above the boiling point of water. It lives at very high pressure, so the sea water is still liquid at that temperature. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremophile\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremophile</a><br /> <br /> Are you looking for a user of Protean who can be put into a light-proof box, with a supply of blood, and survive the rigors of space, unshielded, while being shot to Mars? Teach him about Tardigrades. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tardigrade\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tardigrade </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T22:51:50-07:00","id":1119775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1119694#post1119694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coral and some molluscs are able to create hard, stone-like structures around their bodies. A vampire who is expecting to enter torpor could create such a shell before merging with the earth, making for a very durable haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a similar thing already written as a Protean/Resilience devotion.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mummify</b></span><br /> (Protean \u2022, Resilience \u2022\u2022)</i><br /> By spending a Vitae the vampire may become a dried up husk of herself. This husk is as immobile and unperceptive as the Unmarked Grave and confers the same advantages, including the possibility to switch Protean aspects. Additionally, her mummified skin gains general armor rating equal to her Resilience dots.<br /> This devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-24-2017, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T15:06:21-07:00","id":1120094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1119694#post1119694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Any of the following abilities would need to be written up with game mechanics in mind and might not be possible, anyway, but are worth consideration:</u></div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm... seems to be mostly overlapping with already existing things. Or already redundant with innate aspects of vampirehood. Easily doable already, save the Extreme Environment bit near the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lacking a skeleton might allow squeezing through extremely small openings and would make you virtually impossible to tie up or handcuff. It also ma give the option of enveloping another creature completely. </div> </div> </div> Rubbery Flesh already lets you squeeze through small openings. Enveloping a creature entirely could, depending on what you do with it, be reproduced by the mist form (killing from inside out) or barbed hands (grappling power), or another, depending on what &quot;enveloping&quot; goes for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Carnivorous sponges (which sound like a bad horror movie concept, but exist on the continental shelf off Antarctica) hunt by producing a very sticky substance which traps prey on their surface and then absorb nutrients at their leisure. This sticky stuff is strong enough to hold prey in very cold salt water. If used on dry land, it would make it virtually impossible for prey to escape. </div> </div> </div> Another grappling bonus, ala reflavored Barbed Hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coral and some molluscs are able to create hard, stone-like structures around their bodies. A vampire who is expecting to enter torpor could create such a shell before merging with the earth, making for a very durable haven. </div> </div> </div> There's already an entire discipline that fucntions as vampire-armor, and a devotion for super-torpor protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jellyfish and flatworms often have no heart, using a system distantly similar to peristalsis to push nutrients through their bodies. Some animals have no circulatory system at all; blood (if they have clearly differentiated blood, many just use sea water) just diffuses through their body. How would you stake a vampire with this set-up? </div> </div> </div> There are already several anti-staking abilities in the game. Should protean be able to reproduce an ability that's in another power? We don't want protean to become the everything-power, after all. You could argue for scent glands for a social bonus, but that's stepping on Majesty's territory.<br /> <br /> And, even if you allow it? There are drawbacks to not having a heart, as per the Scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brains are another optional organ, common among vertebrates, but not especially vital among other animals. Some have a bundle of nerves that kind of resemble a brain, some just don't, and contract out all their nerve activity to individual body parts. This is why octopus tentacles keep moving and reacting to touch after removal. If a vampire had this feature, would beheading matter? </div> </div> </div> Does beheading matter now? At best, that's a kind of killing blow situation where massive amounts of damage are bleeding over lethal into agg (thus torpor). There's nothing to suggest that a vampire with its head cut off is any different than any other kind of massive-damage situation.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting a &quot;counter&quot; to something that doesn't exist in the rules in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to start a shouting match at a dinner party full of biologists, take on firm stand on whether there are any animals that do not feel pain. It is... contentious, to say the least. But, for story purposes, it could allow to you argue for using Protean to remove the concept of wound penalties. </div> </div> </div> That's a natural ability of vampires - there's a reason frenzy shuts that off in the first place, and vampires experience it when not frenzying. Rewiring the nervous system won't change that.<br /> <br /> Also, suggesting that wound penalties are entirely associated with pain is a bit of a misnomer. The penalties exist for a number of reasons beyond pain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want some ideas for some immunities to different types of damage, the list is pretty long, just check out the wikipedia article on extremophiles. Picrophilus has an optimal growth pH of .2, approaching the acidity of battery acid. Strain 121 (which arguably would not eligible since it's not quite an animal... it is an Archaean, but...) can reproduce at 121centigrade. Yep, that's well above the boiling point of water. It lives at very high pressure, so the sea water is still liquid at that temperature. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremophile\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremophile</a> </div> </div> </div> Sure, you could go with the anti-Extreme Environment route, but that rarely comes up in a vampire game in the first place. And its entirely possible to do so with existing animals. So, not really something I'd put under &quot;unusual protean forms.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you looking for a user of Protean who can be put into a light-proof box, with a supply of blood, and survive the rigors of space, unshielded, while being shot to Mars? Teach him about Tardigrades. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tardigrade\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tardigrade </a> </div> </div> </div> Umm.... who says you even need protean to begin with? Exposure to a vacuum deals with water vapor forming and expanding in the body. Vitae, by its very nature, won't do that; it lies under a vampires control all the time to the point it can't leak out of the body under any pressure, gravitational, suction, whatever. There's no need of air either, and even the vacuum of space isnt' strong enough to pull non-moisturized flesh apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T16:21:21-07:00","id":1120122,"title":"","content":"One thing I think people often forget with Predatory Aspect:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While every Gangrel\u2019s Beast is different, its<br /> manifestation usually takes inspiration from a predatory or<br /> scavenging animal of some form. </div> </div> </div>supported by:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When she changes adaptation,<br /> the player should work to maintain the theme of a specific<br /> predatory creature \u2014 though she may pick a different predator<br /> to copy when the vampire\u2019s adaptations change. </div> </div> </div>Carnivore sponges probably don't count as &quot;predators&quot; since they don't hunt. And I'm not sure who would want their Beast represented by a sponge anyway. And it's just scavengers and predators, so it's more restrictive than Beast's Skin as to what animals are considered acceptable. Honestly, I don't think tardigrades qualify for either power.<br /> <br /> Protean does have a lot more options than it typically gets used for, but it does still have limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T20:54:59-07:00","id":1120220,"title":"","content":"While these are all really good points, I feel like we're looking at Protean at too much of a Gangrel angle, and while that's fine, it seems a bit unfair to just assume that Protean is exactly the same for the Pijavica as it is for Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T05:03:55-07:00","id":1120313,"title":"","content":"The problem that I feel is going on here is that people are coming up with these different animal features here, and not looking at actual mechanics. Sure, someone who gets suction cup hands for clinging onto people is going to look and act differently from someone who turns into an enveloping liquid, but they're both going to be getting the same exact +Protean dots bonus to grappling. Its easy enough to list a bunch of different animals. Sure. But that is not translating into actual new mechanics. <br /> <br /> I also feel compelled to ask why we're bringing up a wide variety of animals in the first place. The point was to talk about what a giant puddle of blood could do. The Pijavica turn into blood forms, not into little fungus or aquatic sponges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T05:11:30-07:00","id":1120316,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a><br /> <br /> I just want to check that I'm understanding what you're saying. What I'm hearing you say is that there is no reason to expand the palette of animals used for Protean to those not traditionally associated with vampires, because the newly introduced animals have no characteristics that provide a rationale for creating an ability with a substantially different mechanical effect from those already available. In short, don't fix what ain't broke.<br /> <br /> Thing is, though, I'm not suggesting an expansion of the animal palette for the purpose of creating new mechanical effects that don't already have an analogue in the powers of Protean. Rather, what I'm suggesting is that by introducing a new palette of predatory animals more in tune with the themes of the Pijavica, that clan can use the same mechanical effects of Protean as the fur-and-fang Gangrel just with new, parallel, animal traits justifying them. This removes the need to re-jigger Protean to fit the themes of the clan, and gives one possible answer to the original question posted.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> <br /> <br /> The Tardigrade is a predatory animal.<br /> <br /> True, a micro-animal.<br /> <br /> True, not an obligate carnivore.<br /> <br /> However, the way Tardigrades feed is they have a retractable styler, which is a tooth-like mouth part in the shape of a spear, which they extend to breach the cells of algae, mosses and, yes, small invertebrates. They move around with their legs, guided by their senses, using eyes and bristles across their bodies that sense vibration. They move toward their prey, breach it with their styler, and then suck the internal fluids from the target.<br /> <br /> Extendable fangs, used to break the skin of prey and then using their mouth to suck out internal fluids. Sound familiar in a vampire game?<br /> <br /> Now, sponges, lacking motility, seem an odd fit for predatory animals, I admit. But, there are sponges that trap prey and then feed from them in place. They are killing another creature to feed from it's body. That's pretty much the definition of predation.<br /> <br /> If a vampire were, through some horrible mishap, encased up to their neck in concrete, unable to move, but used Dominate or Majesty to hold prey near them, then drank them dry, would that not count as predation? For that matter the ability of vampires using Protean 1 to feed on blood spilled over their internment mirrors the feeding habits of sessile predators.<br /> <br /> I freely admit getting outside of the traditional fur-and-fang angle of Protean gets really weird, really fast. The original topic here, though, was Pijavica and Protean. My point is that, if you consider animals not normally associated with vampires, but still predatory animals, Protean begins to make more sense as a Pijavica discipline.<br /> <br /> And, if you expand the palette of predatory animals available for Protean, the entire Pijavica life-cycle and body plan start to make a <i>lot</i> more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T05:42:01-07:00","id":1120322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120316#post1120316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a><br /> <br /> I just want to check that I'm understanding what you're saying. What I'm hearing you say is that there is no reason to expand the palette of animals used for Protean to those not traditionally associated with vampires, because the newly introduced animals have no characteristics that provide a rationale for creating an ability with a substantially different mechanical effect from those already available. In short, don't fix what ain't broke.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't sound like what he's talking about. He's saying &quot;people discussing Oooh we could make a protean devotion about x animal ability&quot; is pointless when all those things being discussed are already present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T05:45:49-07:00","id":1120324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120316#post1120316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a><br /> <br /> I just want to check that I'm understanding what you're saying. What I'm hearing you say is that there is no reason to expand the palette of animals used for Protean to those not traditionally associated with vampires, because the newly introduced animals have no characteristics that provide a rationale for creating an ability with a substantially different mechanical effect from those already available. In short, don't fix what ain't broke.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I'm saying come up with actual <i><b>mechanics</b></i> instead of just lists of animals. We have a powers for grappling and armor already, so move on from those. We're not creating a &quot;substatially different mechanical effect,&quot; we're repeating what we already have. <br /> <br /> Now, admittedly, the protection from extreme environments is something that doesn't currently exist, which was suggested. That said, extreme environments are very rare in Vampire in the first place, so its very unlikely to come up, but I'm all for it if someone wants it (not fire, though).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm suggesting is that by introducing a new palette of predatory animals more in tune with the themes of the Pijavica, </div> </div> </div> There are no animals in tune with the Pijavica. That's the whole point. The Pijavica are sentient pools of blood. That's their schtick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-25-2017, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T07:55:10-07:00","id":1120352,"title":"","content":"A sponge is a sapient collection of jelly like stem cells that change function according to need and classify as animals. It's not that difficult to draw a line saying they're similiar to shapeshifting puddles of blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T15:22:51-07:00","id":1120519,"title":"","content":"While I agree that focusing on animals so exclusively shouldn't be too much a thing, both clans are very different in terms of Curse, theme, and undead physiology.. I wouldn't say that one shouldn't discount using some animals for very basic inspiration. The Pijavica do have access to Animalism, so they do have a slight influence on animals. But yeah I largely agree with MCN that it's more fitting to look more at flesh warping and blood manipulation for their Protean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T15:27:33-07:00","id":1120521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120352#post1120352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sponge is a sapient collection of jelly like stem cells that change function according to need and classify as animals. It's not that difficult to draw a line saying they're similiar to shapeshifting puddles of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>And maybe one could use that as inspiration for a Blood Form esque replacement for Primeval Miasma or something!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:07:55-07:00","id":1120736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120352#post1120352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sponge is a sapient collection of jelly like stem cells that change function according to need and classify as animals. It's not that difficult to draw a line saying they're similiar to shapeshifting puddles of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, from a thematic standpoint, they're hugely, vastly different. Vampire magic doesn't care about scientific classification. The Pijavica have no thematic common ground with a sponge. They're not sitting in one place, relying on food to come to them because of the flow of a liquid. They ARE the liquid. They're the one constantly flowing and picking up life inside of them.<br /> <br /> As for Animalism? Ventrue aren't animal themed just because they have access to that, so trying to make that link is kind of a stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-26-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:17:30-07:00","id":1120806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120736#post1120736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, from a thematic standpoint, they're hugely, vastly different. Vampire magic doesn't care about scientific classification. The Pijavica have no thematic common ground with a sponge. They're not sitting in one place, relying on food to come to them because of the flow of a liquid. They ARE the liquid. They're the one constantly flowing and picking up life inside of them.<br /> <br /> As for Animalism? Ventrue aren't animal themed just because they have access to that, so trying to make that link is kind of a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said they had an influence on animals, not that they were animal themed. But now that you bring it up, there are at least two or three Ventrue Bloodlines who are heavily themed on animals... so it isn't that much of a stretch. The Curse will steal and appropriate anything useful after all.<br /> <br /> But hey, you have made your point and it is a valid one, let's try to move from this and go back to making Protean unique instead of &quot;Just regular Protean but with nifty Devotions.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-26-2017, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:47:18-07:00","id":1120830,"title":"","content":"Magic vs. &quot;Natural&quot; Biomechanics is irrelevant. The sponge comparison to vampire depends on what themes one is examining. <br /> <br /> Vampires are sponges; they attach themselves to a single location, they feed off anyone or anything that comes in range. They don't leave their domain unless stonger currents push them away. <br /> They suck up water (whole blood is over 80% water) filtering out what they need and spit out the rest. <br /> The entirety of vampiric society entails sponging off human existence, capability, and achievements.<br /> <br /> As for the shapeshifting, sponges also have limited shapeshifting ability by being able to alter the cells in their body to process nutrients and change their appearance to avoid danger or more efficiently obtain food. <br /> <br /> Mobile puddles of blood is not a theme. It's an aesthetic preference appealing to people who think a mass of red ooze slinking around and turning into a blood drinking monster looks cool. <br /> <br /> As for the afterthought clan, I didn't reference the Ventrue at all in this thread so I'm not sure what your point is supposed to be. The Animalism power which requires some contortion to justify saying is about animals, has nothing to do with it. Ventrue can be animal themed because they behave like animals or they can be given a token power affiliated with a specific animal or they decide to call themself that animal type. The same as any other vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:56:59-07:00","id":1120934,"title":"","content":"You can't &quot;make Protean unique&quot; for one Clan. All Disciplines work the same for everyone who has them. A Ventrue or a Nosferatu with Protean works exactly the same as a Gangrel with Protean. I'm not sure why that's suddenly not good enough for this new Clan, when it's always been the case.<br /> <br /> The way you <i>could</i> do this is via Devotions, where you can do pretty much whatever you want. &quot;Just regular Protean but with nifty Devotions&quot; is how it works. No other Clan gets a Discipline changed to fit them. That's not how it works. It's inconsistent with the established setting. If you wanted to make a thread for homebrewing a setting where all Disciplines are affected by the Clan who uses them, that'd be a different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:19:03-07:00","id":1120945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120934#post1120934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't &quot;make Protean unique&quot; for one Clan. All Disciplines work the same for everyone who has them. A Ventrue or a Nosferatu with Protean works exactly the same as a Gangrel with Protean. I'm not sure why that's suddenly not good enough for this new Clan, when it's always been the case.<br /> <br /> The way you <i>could</i> do this is via Devotions, where you can do pretty much whatever you want. &quot;Just regular Protean but with nifty Devotions&quot; is how it works. No other Clan gets a Discipline changed to fit them. That's not how it works. It's inconsistent with the established setting. If you wanted to make a thread for homebrewing a setting where all Disciplines are affected by the Clan who uses them, that'd be a different story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that this isn't the case due to one thing: Protean is not innate to the other clans but the Pijavica and the Gangrel. The reason that Protean functions, in my opinion mind you but it is somewhat supported in game, like it does for the Gangrel when other vampires learn it is because in order TO learn it, they must first drink from a Gangrel and take their Vitae into themselves, and this subtly changes them. As a result, Protean is expressed as the Beast as a primeval predator by every other vampire who learns it because that is how the Gangrel's curse is Expressed. Now with the Pijavica, this is not quite the case, as their Curse is essentially a different strain, therefore it would develop along paths differently in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-26-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:23:05-07:00","id":1120947,"title":"","content":"On another note, finally finished that Devotion I mentioned a couple days ago; I hope you all find it interesting!<br /> <br /> ______<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Carpet of Corruption</b> ( Animalism 2, Protean 4, Resilience 3)<br /> <br /> The Pijavica are masses of blood and viscera that have gained sapience and terrible hunger due to the Embrace, and even though they have attained a human-ish form they never forget the uncertainty of survival as ravenous blobs - they remember what it was like to be less than Kine and Kindred both. But they also remember the strength of such a base form can offer, even if others cannot see the benefit, and the eldest of the Clan can shape the basest of living creatures into a semblance of themselves. With this Devotion the Pijavica have been known to coat their entire havens in thick carpets of ravenous unliving ooze; semi-vampiric colonies of lifeless bacteria, dead skin, or disgusting combinations of the two - perfect for acting as a security measure or a method of ( not so)subtly stealing blood from unsuspecting guests or intruders.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement</b>: Blood must be spread where the user wishes this Devotion to take effect ( included in the activation cost)<br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>: None.<br /> <br /> <b>Duration</b>: A number of nights equal to the User's (Blood Potency * Dots in Animalism *)<br /> <br /> The Pijavica spreads her blood upon whatever surface she wishes to use this Devotion upon, and within the scene colonies of undead micro-organisms and reanimated motes of dust ( which are in fact tiny flakes of dead skin) will begin coalescing upon whichever surface the user marked, smeared across walls and floors like foul smelling slime molds or dangling from the ceiling in streams like some sort of cave-dwelling bacterial colony feeding off of a stalactite. These colony masses behave similarly to more ordinary creatures raised by the second level of Animalism save for the inability to move ( well not quite true, these colonies can attain locomotion, albeit it is extremely slow going, oft to the point of near immobility.) and their lack of sensory apparatus that other, much larger animals possess. What they lack in mobility or traditional senses is mitigated for the purpose that they serve, which is to weaken and steal the blood of those who come in contact with them who are not the user, by manifesting &quot;natural&quot; weapons that emerge from the ooze such as fleshy, rot inducing spines, bone spikes, even beds of jagged fangs or blood sucking tendrils.<br /> <br /> The Carpets of Corruption inflict a number of lethal points of damage ( even to vampires!) equal to the User's Blood Potency upon contact and absorb amount of blood ( or even Vitae) equal to the amount of damage inflicted - though this damage can be avoided by a Dex + Athletics roll - the User's Blood Potency. Like ordinary Familiars these Carpets lack the ability to convert blood into Vitae, should Vitae be absorbed by the colony it may use the stolen lifeforce to sustain itself as if the User had fed it herself, though the duration for which it remains &quot;alive&quot; is determined by the victim's Blood Potency rather than the User. In addition, if more than one point of Vitae has been absorbed, the Carpet may store the rest to be used to sustain the colony when needed unless the User commands otherwise. At any time, the User may coax any colonies who have absorbed any blood or Vitae to exude their cache, allowing her to drink the blood or Vitae as normal ( along with the risks of vinculum or vitae addiction as normal.)<br /> <br /> These colonies are vulnerable to fire and can be easily destroyed with application of flame, and should they not be sustained by their master( or any unlucky vampiric victims) they will die and dissolve once a number of nights equal to the user's ( Blood Potency * Animalism) pass.<br /> <br /> *This alteration is due to it being impossible to quantify Stamina scores for such minuscule creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-26-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T03:47:48-07:00","id":1121246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120947#post1120947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Carpets of Corruption inflict a number of lethal points of damage ( even to vampires!) equal to the User's Blood Potency upon contact and absorb amount of blood ( or even Vitae) equal to the amount of damage inflicted</div> </div> </div> </div>O.O That doesn't feel right. I'd recommend using some other statistic to base the damage on - Blood Potency, being 1 to 10, makes this go from &quot;minor annoyance&quot; to &quot;instant torpor&quot;, which is never a scale you want to use.<br /> <br /> Edit: Love everything else about it, anyway, and will eventually use in my game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T04:17:28-07:00","id":1121253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1120934#post1120934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't &quot;make Protean unique&quot; for one Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, while you can't make it unique, we can at least come up with several variations of Protean 2/4 abilities, or discuss various ways you can reform animals into something other than just animals* with protean 3. The first and last abilities of Protean are pretty static, but the rest are highly customizable. While, really, you can't say other clans can't use these new forms, you can say they're vanishingly small outside of the clan for various reasons. Likely because of the Gangrel mindset.<br /> <br /> * One of the animal entries actually says it can be used for swarm critters. We could discuss the implications of a.. lets say a slime creature using the same rules. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T07:37:18-07:00","id":1121303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1121246#post1121246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O.O That doesn't feel right. I'd recommend using some other statistic to base the damage on - Blood Potency, being 1 to 10, makes this go from &amp;quot;minor annoyance&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;instant torpor&amp;quot;, which is never a scale you want to use.<br /> <br /> Edit: Love everything else about it, anyway, and will eventually use in my game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, you do have a good point. Perhaps the damage is equal to ones dots in Protean. I'll fix that then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T07:42:32-07:00","id":1121304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118006-pijavica-and-protean-discipline-alterations?p=1121253#post1121253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, while you can't make it unique, we can at least come up with several variations of Protean 2/4 abilities, or discuss various ways you can reform animals into something other than just animals* with protean 3. The first and last abilities of Protean are pretty static, but the rest are highly customizable. While, really, you can't say other clans can't use these new forms, you can say they're vanishingly small outside of the clan for various reasons. Likely because of the Gangrel mindset.<br /> <br /> * One of the animal entries actually says it can be used for swarm critters. We could discuss the implications of a.. lets say a slime creature using the same rules. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually what I was getting at to an extent when I was talking about making it unique. And like before when I mentioned Protean being more or less the same for other Kindred due to it being the innate power of Gangrel, I imagine that if you fed from a Pijavica and decided to gain a dot of Protean from them, you could learn how to use their variation of the Discipline.<br /> <br /> *And I realized that later, though I'm not sure what to use for a stamina score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avata